00:15:43,172 --> 00:15:44,891
I mean, there's been times when

251
00:15:45,032 --> 00:15:47,631
I thought I wasn't going
to make it even five days.

252
00:15:47,772 --> 00:15:50,911
So just to win this challenge
would be incredible.

253
00:15:51,052 --> 00:15:53,631
And to know that I have a
chance to get to the final two

254
00:15:53,732 --> 00:15:55,631
and plead my case would be amazing.

255
00:15:57,872 --> 00:15:59,511
Alright. Well, loved ones,

256
00:15:59,652 --> 00:16:01,391
you're going to be cheering
on from the bench today.

257
00:16:01,532 --> 00:16:04,111
I'm going to give everyone
a minute to catch up.

258
00:16:04,252 --> 00:16:07,431
And then Pia, Baden, Harry
we're gonna get to it.

259
00:16:07,572 --> 00:16:09,431
Oh, my goodness, it's
so good to see you.

260
00:16:11,092 --> 00:16:12,391
- Look at my nails.
- I know.

261
00:16:12,492 --> 00:16:14,551
They've been like this since Day 2.

262
00:16:14,652 --> 00:16:16,031
Did you miss me?

263
00:16:30,132 --> 00:16:33,071
- Mate. Thanks, mate.
- Good luck.

264
00:16:36,892 --> 00:16:38,971
- This is gonna be fun, Harry.
- It's not going to be fun.

265
00:16:40,632 --> 00:16:41,632
Did you say it's going to be fun?

266
00:16:41,692 --> 00:16:43,391
A special kind of fun.

267
00:16:48,412 --> 00:16:49,671
Oh, yeah. They feel nice, huh?

268
00:16:49,812 --> 00:16:52,551
Nice and soft, you know, a bit cushy.

269
00:16:56,292 --> 00:16:57,971
Alright, everyone.

270
00:16:58,052 --> 00:16:59,711
Go ahead and grab your handles.

271
00:17:03,892 --> 00:17:06,871
When you're ready, take up
your position on the pedestals.

272
00:17:09,492 --> 00:17:12,071
Get a nice comfortable position

273
00:17:12,172 --> 00:17:13,631
'cause you're gonna be here a while.

274
00:17:15,712 --> 00:17:16,712
For immunity

275
00:17:16,772 --> 00:17:19,231
and a spot in the final two...

276
00:17:20,492 --> 00:17:21,511
..this challenge is now on.

277
00:17:48,978 --> 00:17:51,377
Pretty simple challenge.

278
00:17:51,518 --> 00:17:54,220
In each of those idols you
have 10% of your body weight.

279
00:17:54,744 --> 00:17:57,163
You just need to keep both
feet on those pedestals,

280
00:17:57,264 --> 00:17:58,443
both idols in the air.

281
00:17:59,684 --> 00:18:02,503
But as is often the case in Survivor,

282
00:18:02,644 --> 00:18:05,223
the simple ones can
be the most difficult.

283
00:18:07,464 --> 00:18:10,283
Nothing comfortable about that position.

284
00:18:10,424 --> 00:18:15,123
The pedestals are gonna start
grinding into the soles of your feet.

285
00:18:16,304 --> 00:18:19,523
That discomfort soon is
going to turn into pain.

286
00:18:21,144 --> 00:18:23,043
Then it becomes about pain management.

287
00:18:24,264 --> 00:18:25,923
Mind over matter at that point.

288
00:18:29,144 --> 00:18:30,863
Alright. That's it.
That's all I got to say.

289
00:18:30,944 --> 00:18:32,443
I'll see you guys in four hours.

290
00:18:32,644 --> 00:18:33,644
Hey.

291
00:19:08,384 --> 00:19:10,243
Baden gonna try out Harry's position.

292
00:19:16,184 --> 00:19:18,043
Baden almost knocks himself out.

293
00:19:20,104 --> 00:19:22,043
Just finding somewhere
comfortable, Jonathan.

294
00:19:22,184 --> 00:19:25,583
You really do not want to
slip in this challenge.

295
00:20:02,744 --> 00:20:04,323
Ooh, a little slip from Baden.

296
00:20:05,404 --> 00:20:07,403
Nothing to see here, right?

297
00:20:34,104 --> 00:20:36,123
That's one hour, guys.

298
00:20:41,744 --> 00:20:43,763
What's the record
for the longest challenge?

299
00:20:43,904 --> 00:20:47,083
Six hours and 28 minutes is the record.

300
00:20:48,304 --> 00:20:51,663
- Would they really last that long?
- They've just gotta push through it.

301
00:20:53,864 --> 00:20:56,563
Baden is the only one up there
with a smile right now.

302
00:21:02,464 --> 00:21:04,243
I would have loved to have
done some proper stargazing

303
00:21:04,344 --> 00:21:05,683
while we're standing here, but...

304
00:21:07,604 --> 00:21:09,663
If I look up, I think I might pass out.

305
00:21:09,744 --> 00:21:11,203
I can see, like, three stars.

306
00:21:11,304 --> 00:21:13,303
Yeah. I was looking up before.

307
00:21:16,224 --> 00:21:18,403
You should see it from our
beach, Mum, it's beautiful.

308
00:21:18,544 --> 00:21:20,803
The whole Milky Way,
all the different stars.

309
00:21:20,904 --> 00:21:21,923
Yeah. Wow.

310
00:21:22,064 --> 00:21:25,243
- So many shooting stars.
- Yeah. Excellent.

311
00:21:42,604 --> 00:21:44,963
You know that you can use shooting
stars to determine winds, Jonathan.

312
00:21:45,104 --> 00:21:47,723
- Really.
- Yeah.

313
00:21:47,864 --> 00:21:50,123
Because the trail they leave
drifts with the wind.

314
00:21:50,224 --> 00:21:53,203
Oh, interesting.

315
00:21:53,344 --> 00:21:55,243
He's not actually
normally this talkative.

316
00:21:55,384 --> 00:21:58,043
- Oh, really?
- Yeah. It's a changed person.

317
00:21:58,144 --> 00:21:59,963
He chats a lot, don't you, Bay?

318
00:22:00,104 --> 00:22:02,403
Did I tell you that everyone
calls me 'Bay' here?

319
00:22:02,544 --> 00:22:04,163
- Bay?
- Bay.

320
00:22:04,304 --> 00:22:07,043
- Like 'bay'. Like Chopper Bay?
- Yeah. Like, Bay.

321
00:22:07,144 --> 00:22:08,803
Where else would you rather be?

322
00:22:08,944 --> 00:22:12,043
Honestly, in the middle of Fiji
standing on some torture pegs.

323
00:22:12,184 --> 00:22:13,683
Do you know how much
difference there is, though,

324
00:22:13,824 --> 00:22:16,443
between, like, a dry crunchy
rice and like a risottoey rice?

325
00:22:16,544 --> 00:22:18,203
Oh, my gosh.

326
00:22:18,304 --> 00:22:20,123
Oh, Dad, how did Brighton do?

327
00:22:20,264 --> 00:22:22,603
Did they get relegated?
Or are they safe?

328
00:22:22,744 --> 00:22:24,403
Oh, the stars are back. Thank goodness.

329
00:22:25,744 --> 00:22:29,323
We haven't been in a room
with walls in 49 days, Pia.

330
00:22:29,424 --> 00:22:31,283
Why did we choose to do this?

331
00:22:32,824 --> 00:22:34,243
Ooh. All good, Harry?

332
00:22:34,344 --> 00:22:35,843
Yeah. I'm readjusting.

333
00:22:37,404 --> 00:22:39,683
Is Harrison actually
you're full first name?

334
00:23:00,844 --> 00:23:08,163
Arrgh! Oh...

335
00:23:08,264 --> 00:23:09,463
Ow...

336
00:23:12,104 --> 00:23:14,403
Pia in a serious amount of pain.

337
00:23:16,044 --> 00:23:18,683
- Oh...
- Whoa.

338
00:23:18,824 --> 00:23:20,563
- Harry.
- Harry.

339
00:23:23,344 --> 00:23:25,563
Almost overbalances.

340
00:23:25,664 --> 00:23:26,664
Nice save.

341
00:23:28,284 --> 00:23:29,883
I love you.

342
00:23:44,064 --> 00:23:47,043
Everyone giving it everything.

343
00:23:48,784 --> 00:23:50,763
A lot of pain on Harry's face now.

344
00:23:50,864 --> 00:23:53,103
Ow...

345
00:23:56,104 --> 00:24:00,383
Guys, you've been up
there for five hours.

346
00:24:01,684 --> 00:24:04,283
- Massive effort from everyone
- Good job, everybody.

347
00:24:04,384 --> 00:24:05,523
Well done.

348
00:24:07,124 --> 00:24:08,963
Arrgh! No...

349
00:24:10,624 --> 00:24:12,643
Pia buckled over in pain.

350
00:24:17,264 --> 00:24:21,483
Pia up on her toes, legs
shaking uncontrollably.

351
00:24:23,184 --> 00:24:26,163
Just wondering how much
more of this she can take.

352
00:24:27,304 --> 00:24:29,923
There's nothing but
pure agony on her face.

353
00:24:33,144 --> 00:24:35,283
Hard to watch.

354
00:24:35,384 --> 00:24:37,743
Oh, yeah. It's just hard.

355
00:24:40,484 --> 00:24:42,743
Arms shaking.

356
00:24:48,184 --> 00:24:51,563
Trying to find that inner
strength to keep going.

357
00:24:52,644 --> 00:24:55,603
Hang in there, P, you can do it.

358
00:25:02,344 --> 00:25:05,243
Just hang in there, sweetheart.

359
00:25:05,344 --> 00:25:07,323
Just breathe. Breathe deep.

360
00:25:10,624 --> 00:25:11,963
Just breathe.

361
00:25:30,024 --> 00:25:33,163
Pia in an excruciating
amount of pain now.

362
00:25:44,284 --> 00:25:46,243
Hey, P, sweetie.

363
00:25:46,384 --> 00:25:49,563
I'm not gonna get any
more proud of you, OK?

364
00:25:49,704 --> 00:25:54,643
Alright. so whatever you need
to do, you just do it, OK?

365
00:25:55,744 --> 00:25:58,603
But I love you and I'm
so proud of you, OK?

366
00:25:58,704 --> 00:26:00,323
So you just do your best.

367
00:26:00,424 --> 00:26:02,203
I don't want to go home.

368
00:26:10,224 --> 00:26:12,043
Just hang in there, kiddo. Kiddo.

369
00:26:12,144 --> 00:26:13,463
If you don't want to go home,

370
00:26:13,604 --> 00:26:15,843
just dig deep and hang in there, OK?

371
00:26:16,924 --> 00:26:21,523
Think about the kids and
just work through it.

372
00:26:27,444 --> 00:26:29,323
Just breathe. Just breathe.

373
00:27:02,704 --> 00:27:05,843
Great job. Great job, sweetheart.

374
00:27:07,084 --> 00:27:09,963
Pia really digging deep.

375
00:27:12,984 --> 00:27:14,643
Giving it everything.

376
00:27:33,144 --> 00:27:34,883
Guys, I just want to let you know

377
00:27:35,024 --> 00:27:38,323
you've been up there for
six hours and 30 minutes.

378
00:27:43,584 --> 00:27:44,723
Well done, guys.

379
00:27:44,864 --> 00:27:48,603
You guys officially hold the
record for the longest challenge

380
00:27:48,704 --> 00:27:50,403
in Australian Survivor history.

381
00:27:50,504 --> 00:27:52,243
Wow!

382
00:27:52,344 --> 00:27:54,043
Great job, everybody.

383
00:27:56,784 --> 00:27:58,543
Keep going, Harry.

384
00:27:58,664 --> 00:28:01,163
Now it's about who wants
that necklace the most.

385
00:28:18,144 --> 00:28:22,483
Harry cannot control
the shake in his leg.

386
00:28:39,304 --> 00:28:41,043
Arrgh!

387
00:28:45,164 --> 00:28:47,163
Pia contorted in pain.

388
00:28:59,744 --> 00:29:01,603
- JLP...
- Yeah.

389
00:29:03,444 --> 00:29:05,163
Can you help me get down, please?

390
00:29:12,424 --> 00:29:17,643
And after six hours and 40 minutes,

391
00:29:17,744 --> 00:29:20,683
Harry steps out of the challenge.

392
00:29:20,784 --> 00:29:23,363
Great effort. Take a seat.

393
00:29:26,144 --> 00:29:27,403
Great job, Harry.

394
00:29:28,664 --> 00:29:30,283
It was a great effort.

395
00:29:30,424 --> 00:29:32,843
- Come here.
- Unbelievable effort.

396
00:29:45,544 --> 00:29:49,803
We're left with two, Baden and Pia.

397
00:29:51,444 --> 00:29:52,963
I can't move.

398
00:29:56,704 --> 00:29:59,263
I think I have to get
down. I'm so sorry.

399
00:29:59,404 --> 00:30:01,983
It's OK. Just do whatever
you have to do, sweetheart.

400
00:30:02,064 --> 00:30:03,443
I'm so proud.

401
00:30:03,544 --> 00:30:05,623
I'm trying to get down but I can't.

402
00:30:05,704 --> 00:30:08,483
You want to get down? OK.

403
00:30:10,004 --> 00:30:13,683
After over six hours and 40 minutes...

404
00:30:19,964 --> 00:30:21,803
..that's it, Baden.

405
00:30:30,504 --> 00:30:31,983
Thank you.

406
00:30:33,424 --> 00:30:34,763
Baden, congratulations.

407
00:30:34,864 --> 00:30:36,923
After six hours and 40 minutes...

408
00:30:37,024 --> 00:30:38,723
Wow.

409
00:30:38,864 --> 00:30:42,203
..you have won the final
individual immunity.

410
00:30:42,304 --> 00:30:44,043
Oh, my God.

411
00:30:55,802 --> 00:30:58,421
- Baden, come on over.
- Jonathan.

412
00:31:00,722 --> 00:31:03,281
Turn around. Congratulations.

413
00:31:04,542 --> 00:31:08,101
First individual immunity win,

414
00:31:08,242 --> 00:31:11,281
guaranteed a spot at
that final tribal council

415
00:31:11,422 --> 00:31:13,981
where you will have a chance
to plead your case to the jury.

416
00:31:16,202 --> 00:31:20,821
It's just so special but mostly that
my family were here to see this.

417
00:31:20,922 --> 00:31:23,181
I've come so close so many times

418
00:31:23,282 --> 00:31:26,061
and it just means so much to me

419
00:31:26,162 --> 00:31:28,461
that you guys are here for this one.

420
00:31:29,822 --> 00:31:31,181
One big decision left.

421
00:31:31,322 --> 00:31:34,301
Who are you gonna take
to that final tribal?

422
00:31:34,442 --> 00:31:38,861
And who's gonna join the
jury at the end of tonight?

423
00:31:39,962 --> 00:31:41,061
It's a lot to think about.

424
00:31:41,162 --> 00:31:43,381
It's... That's huge.

425
00:31:43,562 --> 00:31:45,921
- Guys, say goodbye to your loved ones.
- Yep.

426
00:31:46,062 --> 00:31:47,741
And I'll see you guys tonight at tribal.

427
00:31:47,922 --> 00:31:50,941
- See you, Mum. You can hardly walk.
- I know.

428
00:31:51,082 --> 00:31:53,061
I got the victory I've
been craving for so long

429
00:31:53,162 --> 00:31:54,641
and I could not be happier.

430
00:31:54,762 --> 00:31:56,821
Nice to meet you guys. Nice to meet you.

431
00:31:56,962 --> 00:32:00,101
And that's making me skip along
even though my feet are killing me.

432
00:32:01,802 --> 00:32:04,281
But now it's actually kind of terrifying

433
00:32:04,362 --> 00:32:05,941
how much power I hold at the moment.

434
00:32:06,082 --> 00:32:08,781
I have no idea who to
take to the end with me.

435
00:32:08,882 --> 00:32:10,741
And if I make the wrong choice here,

436
00:32:10,882 --> 00:32:13,021
I could be dooming
myself to second place.

437
00:32:13,162 --> 00:32:16,181
This is a half-a-million-dollar choice.

438
00:32:49,162 --> 00:32:51,641
I'll now bring in the
members of our jury.

439
00:32:51,782 --> 00:32:53,541
- Wow.
- Shaun.

440
00:32:53,682 --> 00:32:55,221
- David.
- Wow. Baden's got it.

441
00:32:55,362 --> 00:32:58,181
- John, Daisy...
- My God.

442
00:32:58,282 --> 00:32:59,781
..Simon.

443
00:32:59,922 --> 00:33:01,541
- Janine...
- Oh, my God.

444
00:33:01,642 --> 00:33:02,642
Abbey,

445
00:33:02,682 --> 00:33:05,661
and Luke, voted out
at the last tribal council.

446
00:33:10,942 --> 00:33:15,781
Well, first of all, congratulations,
guys, for breaking the record

447
00:33:15,922 --> 00:33:20,141
for the longest challenge in
Australian Survivor history.

448
00:33:20,242 --> 00:33:21,301
Well done.

449
00:33:21,402 --> 00:33:24,181
But after six hours and 40 minutes

450
00:33:24,322 --> 00:33:29,221
Baden, it was you who walked out
of there wearing that necklace.

451
00:33:30,642 --> 00:33:34,261
Now you have the power to decide
who's going to be in the final two.

452
00:33:34,362 --> 00:33:35,581
Is that weighing on you?

453
00:33:35,682 --> 00:33:38,361
Absolutely it's weighing on me.

454
00:33:38,482 --> 00:33:42,141
It's the sort of power that you can
only dream of having in this game.

455
00:33:42,282 --> 00:33:46,821
And there's definitely two major
things in my mind tonight.

456
00:33:46,962 --> 00:33:49,541
The strength of both
Harry and Pia's games

457
00:33:49,682 --> 00:33:52,861
and what the jury is looking
for in a player at the end.

458
00:33:58,962 --> 00:34:01,181
Alright. Pia.

459
00:34:01,322 --> 00:34:03,421
After the game that you've played so far

460
00:34:03,562 --> 00:34:05,901
and your effort in the challenge today

461
00:34:06,042 --> 00:34:10,501
do you think you deserve to be in
the final two more than Harry does?

462
00:34:10,642 --> 00:34:13,181
I mean, I don't want to say I
deserve to be in the final two

463
00:34:13,282 --> 00:34:14,941
more than Harry does.

464
00:34:15,042 --> 00:34:16,261
But I definitely think

465
00:34:16,402 --> 00:34:20,021
that Baden has a better
shot at winning against me.

466
00:34:26,602 --> 00:34:29,101
These guys have played the game together

467
00:34:29,202 --> 00:34:31,101
and they've made the same moves.

468
00:34:31,242 --> 00:34:33,941
But Harry is a little more strategic.

469
00:34:36,102 --> 00:34:38,621
If you put them both in the final two,

470
00:34:38,762 --> 00:34:42,501
it will be harder for Baden
to own some of those moves.

471
00:34:48,882 --> 00:34:51,461
Harry, what would you say to that?

472
00:34:51,602 --> 00:34:53,741
I think the problem that
just got highlighted there

473
00:34:53,842 --> 00:34:57,261
is that my game is already out there

474
00:34:57,402 --> 00:35:00,741
but I've seen Pia's game
since the tribe swap.

475
00:35:00,842 --> 00:35:03,621
And it's subtle, yes.

476
00:35:03,762 --> 00:35:07,621
But if you think that it's
been a weak game in any way,

477
00:35:07,722 --> 00:35:09,461
then you're dead wrong.

478
00:35:13,102 --> 00:35:16,421
Walking into tomorrow's
tribal if Pia is here,

479
00:35:16,522 --> 00:35:18,081
she's gonna have a lot of surprises.

480
00:35:18,162 --> 00:35:20,181
On top of that,

481
00:35:20,322 --> 00:35:24,621
there's a lot to be gained by
taking a fellow Contender here.

482
00:35:24,762 --> 00:35:26,021
I mean, you just look at the numbers.

483
00:35:26,122 --> 00:35:27,501
There's five Champions

484
00:35:27,642 --> 00:35:32,021
and less than that in
Contenders at the moment.

485
00:35:32,162 --> 00:35:35,341
If you're taking Pia,
you're against the odds.

486
00:35:38,722 --> 00:35:41,341
I will say, though, with the Champions,

487
00:35:41,442 --> 00:35:44,101
there are a few I voted out who,

488
00:35:44,242 --> 00:35:47,221
I mean, actually all of
them except for Janine,

489
00:35:47,322 --> 00:35:50,341
who are not happy with me.

490
00:35:50,482 --> 00:35:53,441
I also didn't spend that much
time with the Contenders

491
00:35:53,562 --> 00:35:56,501
so I'm not sure that there's
a lot of love coming my way.

492
00:35:57,922 --> 00:36:00,301
And you did a really good
job working with Abbey

493
00:36:00,402 --> 00:36:02,821
and that alliance of four.

494
00:36:02,922 --> 00:36:03,941
You bamboozled me a lot

495
00:36:04,082 --> 00:36:06,941
when I was going between,
like, Abbey and everyone

496
00:36:07,042 --> 00:36:08,941
trying to save myself.

497
00:36:09,082 --> 00:36:10,701
I really think there's a better chance

498
00:36:10,802 --> 00:36:12,861
that if you took me you would win.

499
00:36:13,002 --> 00:36:15,901
She sounds very convincing
right now to me.

500
00:36:17,522 --> 00:36:19,101
I'm just saying.

501
00:36:23,182 --> 00:36:26,101
I mean, she is a professional actress

502
00:36:26,242 --> 00:36:29,661
and she's gone through this
game being quite deceptive

503
00:36:29,762 --> 00:36:32,521
about how strong she is.

504
00:36:32,602 --> 00:36:35,181
That's dangerous.

505
00:36:42,682 --> 00:36:45,861
On that note, Baden, you
really have no idea

506
00:36:46,002 --> 00:36:48,941
what these two are planning
to pitch to the jury.

507
00:36:49,042 --> 00:36:51,581
Does that worry you?

508
00:36:51,682 --> 00:36:54,101
It does worry me.

509
00:36:54,242 --> 00:36:55,981
While I'm listening to
what everyone is saying

510
00:36:56,122 --> 00:36:58,741
I can't take everything as being
completely truthful from them

511
00:36:58,882 --> 00:37:03,061
because it benefits their game to
try and convince me to take them.

512
00:37:05,822 --> 00:37:08,581
I mean, I've only known Pia since merge

513
00:37:08,722 --> 00:37:10,621
and I had a bit of a holiday
from Harry in the middle

514
00:37:10,722 --> 00:37:13,061
so I don't know their entire games.

515
00:37:13,162 --> 00:37:14,901
But, um... But...

516
00:37:16,422 --> 00:37:18,181
What was the question again?

517
00:37:23,462 --> 00:37:26,381
Can I just clarify something
and be honest very quickly?

518
00:37:26,482 --> 00:37:28,461
Absolutely.

519
00:37:28,602 --> 00:37:33,541
I told Baden straight out that I
would like to take him to final two.

520
00:37:33,682 --> 00:37:37,461
And that he didn't have to
promise anything to me.

521
00:37:39,242 --> 00:37:43,621
And I said that purely because
I think Pia beats both of us.

522
00:37:46,982 --> 00:37:47,982
Really.

523
00:37:50,542 --> 00:37:52,341
No.

524
00:37:53,802 --> 00:37:57,581
I think if you won today,
you wouldn't have taken me

525
00:37:57,682 --> 00:37:59,741
because you would have taken Baden

526
00:37:59,842 --> 00:38:01,421
because you think you can beat him.

527
00:38:02,542 --> 00:38:06,161
You know that there's a lot of moves
that you feel like you can claim.

528
00:38:10,342 --> 00:38:11,621
We've made some of the same moves

529
00:38:11,762 --> 00:38:14,541
but Baden has made
probably better connections

530
00:38:14,682 --> 00:38:18,261
with a whole lot of
people compared to me.

531
00:38:18,362 --> 00:38:20,701
Baden spent more time with Luke.

532
00:38:20,802 --> 00:38:22,421
Spent more time with Dave.

533
00:38:22,562 --> 00:38:24,941
Spent more time with some
of the old Contenders as well.

534
00:38:25,082 --> 00:38:27,241
But I do think that everyone's
been trying to get you out

535
00:38:27,322 --> 00:38:29,541
and no one's been able to.

536
00:38:31,122 --> 00:38:34,541
I would say that would
be your last big move

537
00:38:34,682 --> 00:38:37,981
to take out the person that everyone
else has tried to take out.

538
00:38:46,962 --> 00:38:48,741
You're willing to bet half
a million dollars on that?

539
00:38:48,882 --> 00:38:51,141
That is the question tonight, isn't it?

540
00:38:57,722 --> 00:39:00,381
OK. So, Harry, Pia, you
can't vote for Baden,

541
00:39:00,522 --> 00:39:02,141
which means you can only
vote for each other

542
00:39:02,282 --> 00:39:04,881
effectively cancelling each other out.

543
00:39:05,002 --> 00:39:08,581
So, Baden, it is your
vote that will decide

544
00:39:08,722 --> 00:39:12,241
who will be leaving this game and
become the final number of our jury.

545
00:39:16,042 --> 00:39:17,741
Baden,

546
00:39:17,842 --> 00:39:19,421
it is time to vote.

547
00:40:27,782 --> 00:40:29,421
I'll collect the vote.

548
00:40:50,722 --> 00:40:53,781
OK. Once the vote is read
the decision is final.

549
00:40:53,882 --> 00:40:55,321
The person voted out

550
00:40:55,462 --> 00:40:57,321
will be asked to leave the
tribal council area immediately.

551
00:40:57,402 --> 00:40:58,541
I'll read the vote.

552
00:41:04,262 --> 00:41:07,661
22nd person voted out
of Australian Survivor,

553
00:41:07,762 --> 00:41:09,661
final member of our jury...

554
00:41:14,062 --> 00:41:15,461
..Harry.

555
00:41:16,842 --> 00:41:18,221
You need to bring me your torch.

556
00:41:18,322 --> 00:41:20,461
Sorry, Harry.

557
00:41:20,602 --> 00:41:23,661
- Don't worry about it.
- It's been amazing, man.

558
00:41:25,122 --> 00:41:26,141
Harry.

559
00:41:29,482 --> 00:41:31,221
We'll see you soon, mate.

560
00:41:33,002 --> 00:41:34,101
Thank you.

561
00:41:39,862 --> 00:41:41,141
Oh! Do it.

562
00:41:43,222 --> 00:41:45,261
Harry, the tribe has spoken.

563
00:41:45,362 --> 00:41:46,621
They sure have.

564
00:41:49,002 --> 00:41:50,341
Time for you to go.

565
00:41:50,482 --> 00:41:53,021
It's been an absolute privilege
to play with all of you.

566
00:41:53,122 --> 00:41:55,581
Like, just an honour.

567
00:41:55,722 --> 00:41:57,861
- Can't wait to see you guys tomorrow.
- See you tomorrow.

568
00:41:58,002 --> 00:42:00,741
- That's exactly right, Harry.
- Give it your best.

569
00:42:04,222 --> 00:42:05,461
Dang.

570
00:42:08,482 --> 00:42:09,821
Well, congratulations.

571
00:42:09,922 --> 00:42:11,961
You are the final two.

572
00:42:13,082 --> 00:42:14,901
You've gone as far as
you can in this game,

573
00:42:15,042 --> 00:42:17,901
and now it's up to these guys, the jury.

574
00:42:19,042 --> 00:42:21,621
So, I suggest go back to
camp, get some rest...

575
00:42:22,802 --> 00:42:24,741
..and think about how you're
going to convince them

576
00:42:24,882 --> 00:42:27,021
that you deserve the
title of Sole Survivor

577
00:42:27,162 --> 00:42:28,781
and the half million that goes with it.

578
00:42:30,402 --> 00:42:32,341
Grab your torches, head on out.

579
00:42:32,442 --> 00:42:33,681
Goodnight.

580
00:43:08,621 --> 00:43:11,385
- Oh, my God, Baden.
- Right.

581
00:43:11,385 --> 00:43:13,344
- I can't believe we did it.
- Final day.

582
00:43:13,344 --> 00:43:14,933
- Look at us.
- Final day.

583
00:43:19,353 --> 00:43:22,242
That will do it. Day 50.

584
00:43:22,242 --> 00:43:24,275
- Pia.
- Final two.

585
00:43:24,275 --> 00:43:26,788
- Congratulations, mate.
- Congratulations, mate.

586
00:43:27,406 --> 00:43:30,205
50 days ago I'd never even built a fire,

587
00:43:30,306 --> 00:43:32,245
but here I am,

588
00:43:32,386 --> 00:43:35,365
one step away from
becoming Sole Survivor.

589
00:43:35,466 --> 00:43:37,285
That's overwhelming to me.

590
00:43:37,426 --> 00:43:40,685
I've been thinking about playing
this game for almost 20 years.

591
00:43:42,546 --> 00:43:45,285
It's my time to take this out.

592
00:43:45,426 --> 00:43:50,245
But also, how many people
get to be this close

593
00:43:50,346 --> 00:43:52,645
to winning half a million dollars?

594
00:43:52,786 --> 00:43:56,465
I mean, I'm not someone
who has a lot of money.

595
00:43:58,586 --> 00:44:01,485
Ever since my first big
role, Looking For Alibrandi,

596
00:44:01,626 --> 00:44:04,605
I've been lucky to work
a lot as an actor.

597
00:44:04,746 --> 00:44:07,525
But I still have to have other
jobs to support myself.

598
00:44:07,626 --> 00:44:08,805
I teach.

599
00:44:08,946 --> 00:44:11,725
This is a small industry
and I do it for the love.

600
00:44:13,906 --> 00:44:15,285
We're a normal Aussie family,

601
00:44:15,426 --> 00:44:18,925
we saved so hard to save
for a deposit for a house.

602
00:44:19,066 --> 00:44:21,565
If I won the money I'd
pay off my mortgage

603
00:44:21,666 --> 00:44:23,525
and have a better life for my kids.

604
00:44:25,946 --> 00:44:28,885
Tonight I'm going into the final tribal.

605
00:44:28,986 --> 00:44:30,485
I get to plead my case to the jury.

606
00:44:32,506 --> 00:44:33,725
If I nail it...

607
00:44:35,206 --> 00:44:38,825
..I could be going home and
changing my kids' lives.

608
00:44:43,646 --> 00:44:45,765
I see a box.

609
00:44:45,906 --> 00:44:48,205
- What is this?
- Oh, my God, Baden!

610
00:44:48,306 --> 00:44:49,485
Food!

611
00:44:49,586 --> 00:44:54,925
Oh, my God, there's bread and eggs.

612
00:44:56,586 --> 00:44:57,825
- Oh, my God.
- Mmm!

613
00:44:57,946 --> 00:45:00,045
I haven't had bread in so
long. Let's go smash it!

614
00:45:00,146 --> 00:45:01,285
Holy cow!

615
00:45:01,426 --> 00:45:03,005
- Oh, my God.
- We're going to be so full.

616
00:45:04,546 --> 00:45:06,765
- Oh, my God. Yummy.
- Yummy.

617
00:45:08,266 --> 00:45:10,205
Imagine how happy Harry
would be if he was here.

618
00:45:10,346 --> 00:45:13,125
Oh, he would be cooking up a feast, eh?

619
00:45:13,266 --> 00:45:15,285
Dammit, should have... No,
I shouldn't have kept him.

620
00:45:17,806 --> 00:45:19,005
Final two feast.

621
00:45:20,466 --> 00:45:22,765
That's a Survivor fan's dream. Isn't it?

622
00:45:24,186 --> 00:45:26,285
- Here's cheers, Pia.
- Cheers.

623
00:45:26,426 --> 00:45:28,045
- Is it OK?
- Mm!

624
00:45:30,866 --> 00:45:32,725
It means more than I can describe

625
00:45:32,866 --> 00:45:35,125
to be able to say that I
made it to the final day

626
00:45:35,266 --> 00:45:37,725
of Australian Survivor, that I
surpassed all these other people.

627
00:45:37,866 --> 00:45:39,825
Who would have thought
us two oddballs...

628
00:45:39,906 --> 00:45:40,906
I know.

629
00:45:40,966 --> 00:45:43,045
Think of the people
that were here, Baden.

630
00:45:43,186 --> 00:45:45,365
All the athletes, all the
strategic masterminds.

631
00:45:45,466 --> 00:45:46,825
We took them.

632
00:45:46,906 --> 00:45:48,765
I just have one more to go

633
00:45:48,906 --> 00:45:51,545
before I can claim the
title of Sole Survivor.

634
00:45:53,826 --> 00:45:56,565
Back in the real world I'm a PhD student

635
00:45:56,706 --> 00:46:00,165
who is introverted, shy,
cautious, risk averse.

636
00:46:00,306 --> 00:46:03,005
I always struggled socially growing up.

637
00:46:03,146 --> 00:46:06,045
I was terrified that one
day I might not belong.

638
00:46:07,566 --> 00:46:09,765
I came into this game
looking to have a shot

639
00:46:09,866 --> 00:46:11,685
and empower people like me.

640
00:46:11,826 --> 00:46:16,605
While Survivor has definitely
pushed me to my limits physically,

641
00:46:16,746 --> 00:46:20,685
I've had to be pushed more than
I've ever pushed myself socially.

642
00:46:22,446 --> 00:46:25,405
I feel like I've transformed.

643
00:46:25,546 --> 00:46:27,845
I've made good connections with people

644
00:46:27,986 --> 00:46:31,365
and used that to be
able to get to the end.

645
00:46:31,506 --> 00:46:33,905
This experience makes
me feel like I belong.

646
00:46:35,546 --> 00:46:38,125
I am the last Contender
left in this game.

647
00:46:39,906 --> 00:46:41,905
The nerds never get a chance
at something like this.

648
00:46:42,026 --> 00:46:44,805
I'm fighting to show that even
your nerdy, awkward person

649
00:46:44,946 --> 00:46:49,685
can come out here, play a social
game and win half a million dollars.

650
00:46:49,826 --> 00:46:52,965
I just need to convince the
jury I deserve the prize

651
00:46:53,066 --> 00:46:55,545
and the title more than Pia.

652
00:46:55,626 --> 00:46:57,565
It's a scary task.

653
00:46:57,706 --> 00:46:59,925
- I can't play for second.
- Nuh.

654
00:47:00,066 --> 00:47:03,125
And I feel like Harry's
game was just so good.

655
00:47:03,226 --> 00:47:04,325
Yeah.

656
00:47:04,466 --> 00:47:07,265
Building up a
resume of good moves,

657
00:47:07,346 --> 00:47:10,245
I made alliances, I made blindsides.

658
00:47:10,386 --> 00:47:14,285
Harry, I took him out because I
looked at his game and my game

659
00:47:14,426 --> 00:47:16,685
and went, "This is the scalp I need."

660
00:47:20,026 --> 00:47:23,445
I do worry that some of them
will see me as a "goat",

661
00:47:23,586 --> 00:47:26,405
someone who has been carried
to the end by others

662
00:47:26,546 --> 00:47:28,485
so that they can be
crushed in the final tribal.

663
00:47:30,286 --> 00:47:32,485
I need to sell the fact that
I've always been playing,

664
00:47:32,586 --> 00:47:34,265
I haven't just watched and waited,

665
00:47:34,386 --> 00:47:37,685
I've actually fought
really hard to be here.

666
00:47:43,386 --> 00:47:46,205
I don't like talking about
myself. I don't like bragging.

667
00:47:47,866 --> 00:47:50,925
But I'm looking tonight to
show that this transformation

668
00:47:51,066 --> 00:47:53,405
is not for nothing and
that to complete it,

669
00:47:53,546 --> 00:47:55,925
the title would be the
ultimate icing on the cake.

670
00:47:57,866 --> 00:48:00,085
- This is it, Pia, 50 days.
- Oh, my God.

671
00:48:00,226 --> 00:48:02,125
Do you know how long
I've wanted to do this?

672
00:48:04,366 --> 00:48:05,645
Goodbye, fire.

673
00:48:08,526 --> 00:48:10,085
Pink and blue.

674
00:48:10,226 --> 00:48:12,165
- One pink, one blue.
- Battle of the ages. Cheers.

675
00:48:12,266 --> 00:48:13,565
Cheers, Pia.

676
00:48:13,706 --> 00:48:16,525
Tonight, there's nine people in
the jury standing between me

677
00:48:16,626 --> 00:48:18,645
and me winning Sole Survivor.

678
00:48:23,666 --> 00:48:25,165
It's a tough pitch.

679
00:48:25,306 --> 00:48:27,165
Baden's got a lot of
friends on that jury

680
00:48:27,306 --> 00:48:30,265
and the only person I didn't
put on that jury was Janine.

681
00:48:31,466 --> 00:48:33,565
That's eight people who I've voted out.

682
00:48:33,706 --> 00:48:35,725
They could easily vote
for him instead of me

683
00:48:35,826 --> 00:48:37,925
because they feel hard done by.

684
00:48:39,106 --> 00:48:42,045
I don't know if it's going to be
a hostile jury or a friendly jury,

685
00:48:42,146 --> 00:48:44,445
but I just have to remind people

686
00:48:44,586 --> 00:48:47,085
that I've played harder
and I should win.

687
00:48:49,346 --> 00:48:51,285
This is more important than
anything I've ever done.

688
00:48:53,586 --> 00:48:55,565
This is the final fight

689
00:48:55,706 --> 00:48:58,365
and I'm ready to give the
performance of my life.

690
00:49:58,311 --> 00:50:00,410
We'll now bring in the
members of our jury.

691
00:50:07,351 --> 00:50:09,610
Shaun, David,

692
00:50:09,711 --> 00:50:11,970
John,

693
00:50:12,071 --> 00:50:13,490
Daisy...

694
00:50:14,651 --> 00:50:16,250
..Simon,

695
00:50:16,351 --> 00:50:17,890
Janine,

696
00:50:17,991 --> 00:50:20,210
Abbey,

697
00:50:20,311 --> 00:50:22,650
Luke and Harry.

698
00:50:22,751 --> 00:50:23,930
Harry!

699
00:50:24,031 --> 00:50:25,970
Voted out at the last tribal council.

700
00:50:33,071 --> 00:50:35,730
Pia, Baden, congratulations.

701
00:50:35,871 --> 00:50:38,930
You guys have gone as far
as you can go in the game.

702
00:50:39,071 --> 00:50:42,170
But tonight, the power
now shifts to the jury.

703
00:50:42,311 --> 00:50:45,290
Nine people you've had a hand
either directly or indirectly

704
00:50:45,391 --> 00:50:46,810
in voting out from this game

705
00:50:46,951 --> 00:50:49,650
will now decide which of
you two deserves the title

706
00:50:49,791 --> 00:50:52,930
of Sole Survivor and the half
million dollars that goes with it.

707
00:50:54,271 --> 00:50:57,770
Now, in a moment you'll each
make an opening statement.

708
00:50:57,911 --> 00:51:00,550
This is your chance to pitch to the jury

709
00:51:00,691 --> 00:51:03,290
why you think you
deserve to win this game.

710
00:51:03,391 --> 00:51:05,690
The jury will then address you.

711
00:51:05,831 --> 00:51:08,450
They'll ask you questions
and you'll answer them,

712
00:51:08,591 --> 00:51:11,910
and then they'll have a chance
to respond to your answers

713
00:51:11,991 --> 00:51:14,170
in an open forum.

714
00:51:14,271 --> 00:51:16,050
Once everyone's said their piece,

715
00:51:16,151 --> 00:51:18,450
the jury will then go up to vote

716
00:51:18,551 --> 00:51:21,090
to decide who will win this game.

717
00:51:22,171 --> 00:51:23,270
You guys ready?

718
00:51:25,591 --> 00:51:26,730
Yeah.

719
00:51:27,871 --> 00:51:29,090
Ready as I'll ever be.

720
00:51:30,291 --> 00:51:32,410
Baden, take it away.

721
00:51:37,511 --> 00:51:38,810
OK, here we go.

722
00:51:38,911 --> 00:51:39,970
Um...

723
00:51:43,391 --> 00:51:46,890
I came into this game as
someone who thought that

724
00:51:47,031 --> 00:51:49,650
applying for Survivor
was a terrifying thing.

725
00:51:49,751 --> 00:51:54,010
I came in super-awkward, super-shy.

726
00:51:56,351 --> 00:51:58,330
I couldn't be the challenge beast

727
00:51:58,471 --> 00:52:00,050
that somehow I got called at some point.

728
00:52:01,431 --> 00:52:04,770
I didn't want to be the orchestrator
of the big strategic moves.

729
00:52:06,631 --> 00:52:10,570
I knew that my best bet
was to play from the middle.

730
00:52:13,151 --> 00:52:16,330
Get into good relationships
with as many people as possible

731
00:52:16,471 --> 00:52:18,270
and hold as much information as I could.

732
00:52:20,071 --> 00:52:24,070
I knew what the plays were going
into every single tribal council.

733
00:52:27,451 --> 00:52:28,890
Just after tribe swap

734
00:52:29,031 --> 00:52:32,210
I could see the
Contenders' strong alliance

735
00:52:32,311 --> 00:52:33,810
was not going to last forever.

736
00:52:33,951 --> 00:52:37,090
I started to make inroads
with the Champions,

737
00:52:37,191 --> 00:52:38,530
and that started with Luke.

738
00:52:40,091 --> 00:52:41,890
Once you get to merge,

739
00:52:41,991 --> 00:52:44,890
I had the inroads with Luke and Dave

740
00:52:45,031 --> 00:52:48,630
so that I had access to some
information from the Champions,

741
00:52:48,751 --> 00:52:50,450
enough to keep myself
off the chopping block

742
00:52:50,551 --> 00:52:52,130
as the Contenders crumbled.

743
00:52:53,351 --> 00:52:57,630
In my mind, in this game, once you
get into the leader position

744
00:52:57,771 --> 00:53:00,210
you have a very short amount of time
before you're kicked out of it,

745
00:53:00,311 --> 00:53:01,450
normally out of the game entirely.

746
00:53:02,871 --> 00:53:05,850
So my goal was to get into
that position as late as possible

747
00:53:05,991 --> 00:53:09,130
and sit there at the end
with the power.

748
00:53:10,931 --> 00:53:13,130
And that's what I did
at the very final challenge.

749
00:53:14,291 --> 00:53:16,890
I knew that Harry would have
taken me to the final two

750
00:53:17,031 --> 00:53:19,850
and Pia would have taken me to
the final two, so why did I fight?

751
00:53:19,991 --> 00:53:23,370
Why didn't I just step down and save
myself the pain and the torture?

752
00:53:23,511 --> 00:53:25,370
I did it because I needed that scalp.

753
00:53:25,511 --> 00:53:28,490
I needed that big resume filler
at the end

754
00:53:28,631 --> 00:53:31,530
to finish off this game
and take control of the game

755
00:53:31,631 --> 00:53:32,770
right when it mattered most.

756
00:53:34,591 --> 00:53:37,530
I understand that you might see my
game as something as more passive...

757
00:53:39,431 --> 00:53:40,730
..but the moves are there,

758
00:53:40,871 --> 00:53:44,530
and the move to intentionally stay
in the middle from beginning to end

759
00:53:44,631 --> 00:53:46,010
is my claim to fame.

760
00:53:47,731 --> 00:53:49,010
And I will own it tonight.

761
00:53:58,231 --> 00:53:59,290
Pia...

762
00:54:00,831 --> 00:54:02,490
..what would you like to say
to the jury?

763
00:54:05,031 --> 00:54:06,031
Hi.

764
00:54:09,971 --> 00:54:11,350
I came into this game

765
00:54:11,471 --> 00:54:13,610
knowing that I was going to play
a social game.

766
00:54:13,751 --> 00:54:15,570
You know, I wasn't going
to be the strongest,

767
00:54:15,711 --> 00:54:18,010
but I knew that what I wanted to do

768
00:54:18,151 --> 00:54:22,250
was be underestimated but
always be fiercely strategic.

769
00:54:23,591 --> 00:54:28,650
Unfortunately I was thrown into a
tribe of very accomplished athletes.

770
00:54:30,231 --> 00:54:33,890
Everyone wanted me out of there
because I wasn't athletic enough.

771
00:54:33,991 --> 00:54:36,530
I really had to play hard.

772
00:54:36,631 --> 00:54:38,450
I worked on Nova

773
00:54:38,591 --> 00:54:42,350
and she changed the vote to
Anastasia and it saved me.

774
00:54:42,491 --> 00:54:44,970
And then I really quickly
had to make alliances,

775
00:54:45,071 --> 00:54:46,530
so I made an alliance of four.

776
00:54:47,791 --> 00:54:51,810
And then we got Abbey and Roscoe
to switch to an alliance of six

777
00:54:51,911 --> 00:54:53,210
and we did dominate.

778
00:54:54,791 --> 00:54:58,130
We went to a tribe swap
and Janine became the Godmother

779
00:54:58,231 --> 00:55:00,130
and I became the Smiling Assassin.

780
00:55:01,831 --> 00:55:06,090
I went to a merge and we did
organise a blindside against Dave.

781
00:55:08,831 --> 00:55:11,610
When finally my alliance
did turn on me...

782
00:55:13,271 --> 00:55:14,810
..I knew that when people
were coming for me

783
00:55:14,951 --> 00:55:17,250
I wanted to have a buffer of
strong people around me,

784
00:55:17,351 --> 00:55:18,810
so they'd come for them first.

785
00:55:20,031 --> 00:55:21,850
That buffer worked

786
00:55:21,991 --> 00:55:24,250
because you came for Simon first
and then Janine.

787
00:55:25,911 --> 00:55:28,610
I put most of you on that jury
except for you, Janine.

788
00:55:29,751 --> 00:55:31,430
I did go to 20 tribal councils,

789
00:55:31,551 --> 00:55:35,330
my name only came up in four
and I was never under threat.

790
00:55:35,471 --> 00:55:38,330
I was always that slippery
little sucker that was there

791
00:55:38,471 --> 00:55:40,850
and you didn't know you needed
to get me until it was too late.

792
00:55:40,991 --> 00:55:45,250
As lovers of Survivor, I hope
that you will vote for the person

793
00:55:45,351 --> 00:55:46,890
who played the best strategic game,

794
00:55:47,031 --> 00:55:50,010
and I think we all know 100%
that that was me.

795
00:55:52,071 --> 00:55:55,290
To vote for me as Sole Survivor
could change my life,

796
00:55:55,391 --> 00:55:57,170
my family's life.

797
00:55:57,311 --> 00:56:01,930
It was a joy to play with you all
and I thank you.

798
00:56:02,031 --> 00:56:03,290
Thanks.

799
00:56:10,311 --> 00:56:12,650
Alright, jury, you've heard
their pitches.

800
00:56:12,751 --> 00:56:15,170
Now it's your turn to ask questions.

801
00:56:20,151 --> 00:56:22,370
Shaun, would you like to kick it off?

802
00:56:22,511 --> 00:56:24,110
- Guys.
- Hi.

803
00:56:24,251 --> 00:56:25,790
- Hey, Shaun.
- Congratulations.

804
00:56:25,911 --> 00:56:28,970
It's an amazing effort to go
50 days, you know, for anyone,

805
00:56:29,111 --> 00:56:31,730
let alone, I guess, an actress
and a PhD student

806
00:56:31,831 --> 00:56:33,370
who barely leaves his room.

807
00:56:35,191 --> 00:56:38,010
But with no bullshit, no digressing,

808
00:56:38,151 --> 00:56:42,250
I want to hear why you think the
other person doesn't deserve to win.

809
00:56:42,391 --> 00:56:44,230
And I think I'd like to start with Pia.

810
00:56:47,371 --> 00:56:51,010
Well, firstly, if you're looking
to vote for the person

811
00:56:51,151 --> 00:56:54,430
who had the best personal growth
and who learned how to make friends

812
00:56:54,611 --> 00:56:57,170
and had a good time out here, then you
absolutely should vote for Baden.

813
00:56:58,691 --> 00:56:59,970
But you cannot vote for Baden

814
00:57:00,111 --> 00:57:02,050
if you're voting for
the best strategic player.

815
00:57:05,231 --> 00:57:07,690
I don't think Baden played
a strategic game at all.

816
00:57:07,831 --> 00:57:11,650
I think he just sat next
to people who were really clever

817
00:57:11,791 --> 00:57:14,250
and they kept him around
because he was an easy person

818
00:57:14,351 --> 00:57:15,650
who would do what they said.

819
00:57:19,271 --> 00:57:22,850
I would counter that
by saying that in my mind

820
00:57:22,991 --> 00:57:25,970
your game has been you've worked
yourself into an alliance early on

821
00:57:26,111 --> 00:57:28,410
and you rode that alliance
until it faltered.

822
00:57:29,951 --> 00:57:31,890
You've been blindsided twice in a row

823
00:57:32,031 --> 00:57:33,610
and then you've been taken through
to the final...

824
00:57:33,751 --> 00:57:35,970
I wasn't blindsided twice. I knew
Janine was getting voted out.

825
00:57:37,331 --> 00:57:38,730
You only say that afterwards.

826
00:57:40,171 --> 00:57:42,090
Like, where's the evidence that...
No, I said it then.

827
00:57:42,191 --> 00:57:43,210
I said it then, that night.

828
00:57:43,351 --> 00:57:46,010
You said it that night,
that you knew that Janine was going?

829
00:57:46,151 --> 00:57:48,290
She actually said to me,
she turned to me and went,

830
00:57:48,431 --> 00:57:50,610
"Mate, we're screwed,
and it's probably you."

831
00:57:50,711 --> 00:57:56,530
Um...

832
00:57:58,031 --> 00:58:00,170
..sitting here with a jury
that probably has

833
00:58:00,311 --> 00:58:01,930
some of the biggest challenge threats

834
00:58:02,071 --> 00:58:05,570
and biggest strategic players
in the history of Survivor...

835
00:58:09,271 --> 00:58:11,810
..personally I both consider
you guys goats.

836
00:58:15,751 --> 00:58:19,150
I would like to hear the truth
on how you think your goat game

837
00:58:19,231 --> 00:58:21,850
was advantageous to you,

838
00:58:21,951 --> 00:58:23,810
and how did that get you to the end?

839
00:58:32,251 --> 00:58:33,810
A goat is someone who follows.

840
00:58:35,591 --> 00:58:37,010
I definitely didn't follow people.

841
00:58:38,591 --> 00:58:42,130
If you are calling me goat, like,
does me blindsiding you not count?

842
00:58:46,391 --> 00:58:47,930
The girls will back me up.

843
00:58:48,071 --> 00:58:50,510
Janine, Abbey and myself were
the ones who thought of it

844
00:58:50,631 --> 00:58:54,530
back at Contenders' camp where
Dave was gunning for Daisy.

845
00:58:55,971 --> 00:58:57,230
I told the girls, and I said,

846
00:58:57,351 --> 00:58:59,190
let's not wait to get you
before you got us.

847
00:59:00,691 --> 00:59:02,230
I worked on Johnno and Harry.

848
00:59:03,431 --> 00:59:06,230
So I had a really big hand
in voting Dave out,

849
00:59:06,311 --> 00:59:08,130
but I had to be careful

850
00:59:08,271 --> 00:59:11,690
because what happens when you
are at the forefront of moves?

851
00:59:11,791 --> 00:59:13,330
You get voted out.

852
00:59:14,471 --> 00:59:15,770
Dave,

853
00:59:15,911 --> 00:59:19,370
you need to know where to sit
and how to make big moves

854
00:59:19,511 --> 00:59:22,970
without being at the forefront
because this is Australian Survivor

855
00:59:23,111 --> 00:59:25,090
and it's very different
to American Survivor.

856
00:59:25,231 --> 00:59:28,810
And in Australia, if we see
someone taking control,

857
00:59:28,951 --> 00:59:30,650
you're going to end up
sitting on the jury.

858
00:59:30,751 --> 00:59:32,290
That's why you're there.

859
00:59:33,671 --> 00:59:37,230
Dave, what I did not do is sit
at the back of an alliance,

860
00:59:37,371 --> 00:59:39,250
at the bottom and
not make any decisions.

861
00:59:42,691 --> 00:59:43,691
I'm not a goat.

862
00:59:43,831 --> 00:59:45,690
I'm a hard-playing Survivor
and I deserve to be here.

863
00:59:48,991 --> 00:59:51,870
And you think that I just sat and watched
every decision be made and didn't...

864
00:59:52,011 --> 00:59:53,530
- I don't know your game well enough.
- OK.

865
00:59:56,711 --> 01:00:00,930
I've put my piece many times in
groups of how I want the vote to go.

866
01:00:01,031 --> 01:00:02,170
Sure.

867
01:00:05,691 --> 01:00:08,530
Um... I'm not a goat.

868
01:00:10,471 --> 01:00:12,250
I made moves. I...

869
01:00:14,951 --> 01:00:18,410
I looked at the people coming
into the endgame and I thought,

870
01:00:18,551 --> 01:00:22,370
"Who here do I have the best chance
of beating at the end?"

871
01:00:22,511 --> 01:00:24,010
You look at Abbey, she's
a challenge threat,

872
01:00:24,151 --> 01:00:26,690
she's played some great moves, she's
moved from alliances to alliances

873
01:00:26,831 --> 01:00:29,810
at the right time to
keep herself above water.

874
01:00:29,951 --> 01:00:32,170
Look at Luke, all the immunity
wins, idols and advantages

875
01:00:32,271 --> 01:00:33,610
all the strategy.

876
01:00:33,751 --> 01:00:35,930
And Look at Harry, he's also
played two idols perfectly

877
01:00:36,031 --> 01:00:38,450
and played an incredibly wily game.

878
01:00:40,391 --> 01:00:43,890
So I pegged my mark and
I said that... to myself

879
01:00:44,031 --> 01:00:46,770
that if I had the choice I
would want Pia at the end.

880
01:00:48,711 --> 01:00:50,890
But Baden, you didn't choose
to take me to the end,

881
01:00:51,031 --> 01:00:52,730
you chose to vote me out and not Abbey.

882
01:00:52,871 --> 01:00:55,610
So, clearly you wanted to take
Abbey to the end instead of me.

883
01:00:55,751 --> 01:00:57,130
Wait, when did I choose to vote you out?

884
01:01:00,611 --> 01:01:03,090
When Luke sent you away
from tribal council

885
01:01:03,231 --> 01:01:05,130
you were going to vote
my name, not Abbey,

886
01:01:05,271 --> 01:01:08,370
so clearly you didn't choose to take
me to the end from the beginning.

887
01:01:11,191 --> 01:01:12,690
So that's not true.

888
01:01:36,581 --> 01:01:39,400
I looked at the people
coming into the end game

889
01:01:39,581 --> 01:01:43,880
and I thought, "Who here do I have the
best chance of beating at the end?"

890
01:01:44,021 --> 01:01:48,160
So I pegged my mark and
I said that, to myself,

891
01:01:48,301 --> 01:01:52,040
that if I had the choice I
would want Pia at the end.

892
01:01:52,181 --> 01:01:54,440
But Baden, you didn't choose
to take me to the end,

893
01:01:54,581 --> 01:01:57,600
you chose to vote me out not
Abbey, so that's not true.

894
01:02:04,521 --> 01:02:06,560
Bay, I just would like
to ask you directly

895
01:02:06,701 --> 01:02:08,600
do you think you played
a good social game?

896
01:02:08,741 --> 01:02:10,760
Yes, absolutely, I played
a good social game.

897
01:02:10,901 --> 01:02:13,720
I made sure that I had good
relationships with everyone.

898
01:02:13,861 --> 01:02:17,300
I made sure that when it came
time to pick off Contenders

899
01:02:17,421 --> 01:02:20,300
that I was seen as someone
that you didn't wanna get rid of.

900
01:02:20,381 --> 01:02:23,480
I mean... My... I own my game.

901
01:02:23,581 --> 01:02:25,200
I played from the middle.

902
01:02:25,341 --> 01:02:28,320
Do you know how hard it is to manage
multiple alliances at the same time

903
01:02:28,461 --> 01:02:30,600
and stop them from both turning on you?

904
01:02:31,821 --> 01:02:36,000
There's a perception that I am
the person that you wanna take

905
01:02:36,141 --> 01:02:37,720
because I won't be able
to put up a good fight

906
01:02:37,861 --> 01:02:39,680
but I have... I'm
putting up a good fight.

907
01:02:39,781 --> 01:02:41,720
I think that I can take Pia,

908
01:02:41,821 --> 01:02:43,240
it's not a foregone conclusion here.

909
01:02:45,261 --> 01:02:48,680
I've had to move from alliance
to alliance from group to group,

910
01:02:48,821 --> 01:02:51,720
I didn't just ride one
alliance until it faltered.

911
01:02:53,741 --> 01:02:57,040
And I've managed to do it in a way
where it's gotten me to the end.

912
01:03:01,041 --> 01:03:03,440
I've gotta say, Pia...

913
01:03:03,581 --> 01:03:06,480
..as a social player, I think
you're a social superwoman.

914
01:03:06,581 --> 01:03:08,200
You are off the charts.

915
01:03:08,301 --> 01:03:09,920
Thank you.

916
01:03:11,221 --> 01:03:12,840
I was actually genuinely scared of you

917
01:03:12,981 --> 01:03:14,680
because I thought, "My God,
please don't target me

918
01:03:14,781 --> 01:03:16,920
"because you are seriously scary."

919
01:03:17,061 --> 01:03:20,120
I see you as the wolf
in goat's clothing.

920
01:03:22,681 --> 01:03:26,320
You were the reason why myself,
and I believe Abbey, got so far.

921
01:03:27,841 --> 01:03:29,380
You were ruthless.

922
01:03:29,521 --> 01:03:33,840
My question is can you please give
myself and this group some examples

923
01:03:34,021 --> 01:03:37,200
of where the Smiling Assassin really
convinced people they're safe.

924
01:03:41,181 --> 01:03:43,680
In the first half of the game,

925
01:03:43,821 --> 01:03:46,320
almost every single
person who I voted out

926
01:03:46,421 --> 01:03:47,720
thought I was their best friend

927
01:03:47,861 --> 01:03:49,320
and they came up to me
just before the vote

928
01:03:49,421 --> 01:03:50,840
and said, "Are you voting for me?"

929
01:03:50,981 --> 01:03:53,560
And I said, "Oh, my God, no,
never." And I voted them out.

930
01:03:57,001 --> 01:03:59,120
Like Susie, everyone, Nova...

931
01:03:59,221 --> 01:04:00,740
I mean, Nova was a big one,

932
01:04:00,861 --> 01:04:02,560
I sat there and had to
really make her happy

933
01:04:02,661 --> 01:04:04,520
just before we blindsided her.

934
01:04:04,661 --> 01:04:07,800
So I could have real
relationships with people

935
01:04:07,941 --> 01:04:10,680
but I had no problem in separating
my relationships with people

936
01:04:10,781 --> 01:04:12,440
and the game.

937
01:04:12,581 --> 01:04:16,020
I really did work on making sure
people who were getting blindsided

938
01:04:16,161 --> 01:04:17,880
didn't know they were
getting blindsided.

939
01:04:18,021 --> 01:04:19,740
I'll vouch for you on that too

940
01:04:19,861 --> 01:04:23,100
I think the conversation I had
before my blindside was, ah...

941
01:04:23,281 --> 01:04:26,920
Yeah, made me feel a little too... too
comfortable, unfortunately.

942
01:04:27,061 --> 01:04:29,160
Comfortable enough to
walk home with an idol.

943
01:04:29,301 --> 01:04:32,440
Yeah. It was, pretty, you
know, pretty big for me.

944
01:04:34,261 --> 01:04:35,740
Harry.

945
01:04:35,821 --> 01:04:38,320
OK...

946
01:04:38,421 --> 01:04:40,240
It's quite clear that...

947
01:04:40,381 --> 01:04:43,520
..to use the analogy of, like,
drivers and passengers,

948
01:04:43,661 --> 01:04:46,800
these two both, they're not
ever in the driver's seat

949
01:04:46,941 --> 01:04:50,380
but they're the person beside
them sort of navigating.

950
01:04:50,521 --> 01:04:53,760
The thing that I think is really
important from both of you

951
01:04:53,901 --> 01:04:57,100
is that there is a fine
line between navigator...

952
01:04:59,001 --> 01:05:00,120
..and passenger.

953
01:05:01,821 --> 01:05:04,760
And you're really gonna
have to articulate that.

954
01:05:07,341 --> 01:05:11,000
I have played a game where I
have controlled what people did.

955
01:05:11,141 --> 01:05:13,200
I'm whispering in people's
ears, making suggestions,

956
01:05:13,301 --> 01:05:14,840
steering them away from things.

957
01:05:14,941 --> 01:05:16,320
Like, when we coming into merge,

958
01:05:16,461 --> 01:05:19,440
I made sure that it was Dave who
was having the hate not Luke,

959
01:05:19,541 --> 01:05:21,160
because I was working with Luke

960
01:05:21,261 --> 01:05:23,320
and I pushed for that to be the case.

961
01:05:24,561 --> 01:05:26,320
I was a part of many moves.

962
01:05:26,461 --> 01:05:29,680
I never stepped into the driver's seat

963
01:05:29,821 --> 01:05:33,480
but I didn't get
blindsided once by a result.

964
01:05:33,621 --> 01:05:38,120
And I don't think that Pia can
say that, in complete truth.

965
01:05:38,261 --> 01:05:40,600
- No, I definitely got blindsided.
- Yeah, exactly.

966
01:05:40,741 --> 01:05:44,520
And then, at the end, you've not been
able to make the ultimate choice

967
01:05:44,621 --> 01:05:46,100
about who to take with you.

968
01:05:48,101 --> 01:05:51,040
Sure. But I didn't magically
appear here tonight.

969
01:05:51,181 --> 01:05:53,360
- No, I'm not saying that.
- I'm here because I played hard,

970
01:05:53,501 --> 01:05:55,880
because when my alliance
faltered, I knew it was coming

971
01:05:55,981 --> 01:05:57,360
and I worked out how to save myself.

972
01:05:58,861 --> 01:06:00,800
Having an alliance is not a weakness,

973
01:06:00,941 --> 01:06:02,920
sticking with your alliance
is not a weakness.

974
01:06:03,061 --> 01:06:05,600
Making big decisions at the
forefront of your alliance

975
01:06:05,701 --> 01:06:07,200
is not a weakness.

976
01:06:07,301 --> 01:06:10,240
I had to work out how to be strong,

977
01:06:10,381 --> 01:06:11,800
how to be on the right side of votes,

978
01:06:11,941 --> 01:06:14,680
how to manipulate votes without
people knowing I was doing it

979
01:06:14,821 --> 01:06:18,200
and how to get people on the jury
without getting a target on my back.

980
01:06:19,821 --> 01:06:23,240
I've worked with each and every
one of you on at least one vote

981
01:06:23,341 --> 01:06:25,680
whether directly or indirectly.

982
01:06:25,821 --> 01:06:29,680
My game was about
sitting in the position

983
01:06:29,781 --> 01:06:31,880
where I had access to information.

984
01:06:32,021 --> 01:06:35,240
I worked with alliances that
were working really well

985
01:06:35,381 --> 01:06:38,920
and my alliances rallied
and we dominated.

986
01:06:39,061 --> 01:06:43,460
But I think my game was something
that was enjoyable to be around.

987
01:06:43,601 --> 01:06:47,240
I was someone who was
willing to vote anyone out.

988
01:06:47,381 --> 01:06:50,120
I would do it with a smile on my face

989
01:06:50,261 --> 01:06:52,040
if it meant that I would get further.

990
01:07:00,341 --> 01:07:01,680
John.

991
01:07:03,821 --> 01:07:07,040
We all came into the
game with a strategy,

992
01:07:07,181 --> 01:07:09,600
be the beast, social
or strategy, whatever.

993
01:07:10,981 --> 01:07:15,180
How did your social game make
you have to adapt throughout?

994
01:07:17,941 --> 01:07:21,320
I've gone from being
this awkward shy person

995
01:07:21,421 --> 01:07:23,200
to someone who's played a game

996
01:07:23,341 --> 01:07:26,720
where people have not
wanted to get rid of me.

997
01:07:27,861 --> 01:07:29,880
I've changed in this game.

998
01:07:31,201 --> 01:07:33,520
I'm here, not just for me,

999
01:07:33,661 --> 01:07:37,120
but people like me who feel that
they're a bit introverted or shy

1000
01:07:37,261 --> 01:07:40,180
and now I'm here, pleading
my case to you guys.

1001
01:07:41,541 --> 01:07:45,760
I've played an ultimate game
of sitting right in the middle.

1002
01:07:48,781 --> 01:07:51,180
I was seen as someone
who was more malleable,

1003
01:07:51,301 --> 01:07:52,820
more able to be worked
on than the others.

1004
01:07:53,981 --> 01:07:56,760
To get to the end, you need to know
when the time is right to strike

1005
01:07:56,861 --> 01:07:58,600
and when the time is right to hold.

1006
01:08:00,101 --> 01:08:02,960
And I made sure that I struck at
the time at the end of the game

1007
01:08:03,101 --> 01:08:05,040
so that there wasn't a
chance to be picked off.

1008
01:08:10,521 --> 01:08:12,180
Alright, Luke,

1009
01:08:12,261 --> 01:08:14,000
it's gonna be lucky last.

1010
01:08:15,221 --> 01:08:16,840
Do you have a question?

1011
01:08:21,781 --> 01:08:23,800
I'll just go to P...

1012
01:08:23,941 --> 01:08:28,840
ah, look, I like to think that I
helped save you twice in the game.

1013
01:08:30,341 --> 01:08:33,120
It's obviously got to,
like, where you are now.

1014
01:08:34,561 --> 01:08:37,560
I would've loved to have
that favour repaid.

1015
01:08:40,441 --> 01:08:41,640
It wasn't.

1016
01:08:44,141 --> 01:08:46,240
Why should I give you my vote?

1017
01:08:53,921 --> 01:08:55,280
Luke...

1018
01:08:58,421 --> 01:09:02,040
..voting you out was one of
the hardest things I had to do

1019
01:09:02,141 --> 01:09:03,840
because I know we've spoken about

1020
01:09:03,981 --> 01:09:06,200
how much we wanted to
win this for our families

1021
01:09:06,301 --> 01:09:09,600
and I will never get over...

1022
01:09:09,741 --> 01:09:11,920
..having to take that
dream away from you.

1023
01:09:13,381 --> 01:09:16,760
Last night, when I was standing on that
podium for 6 hours and 40 minutes,

1024
01:09:16,901 --> 01:09:21,280
I wasn't doing it so that
I could break a record,

1025
01:09:21,381 --> 01:09:23,600
I was doing it so that...

1026
01:09:23,741 --> 01:09:26,240
..if I took away your chance to be here,

1027
01:09:26,381 --> 01:09:29,000
I was gonna make damn sure
that I was here instead.

1028
01:09:30,501 --> 01:09:33,960
Because I didn't want voting
you out to be futile.

1029
01:09:35,921 --> 01:09:38,760
As much as I love working with
Harry I knew that if Harry won,

1030
01:09:38,861 --> 01:09:40,640
I was not gonna be sitting here

1031
01:09:40,781 --> 01:09:43,560
so I was ready to die up on that thing.

1032
01:09:46,281 --> 01:09:49,260
I think I played a great game.

1033
01:09:49,341 --> 01:09:51,040
I didn't have the best physical game

1034
01:09:51,181 --> 01:09:55,320
but in every single challenge, I
pushed myself to the absolute limits

1035
01:09:55,461 --> 01:09:59,040
to help my team, to be a good teammate.

1036
01:10:00,521 --> 01:10:02,200
Yes, I voted some of you out...

1037
01:10:03,461 --> 01:10:05,720
..but my game was a
really good social game,

1038
01:10:05,821 --> 01:10:07,080
it was a strategic game.

1039
01:10:07,221 --> 01:10:09,160
I certainly wasn't someone
who was sitting around,

1040
01:10:09,301 --> 01:10:11,040
waiting for people to
tell me what to do.

1041
01:10:11,181 --> 01:10:13,680
I was always at the forefront
of making decisions.

1042
01:10:15,701 --> 01:10:19,160
Just because I wasn't playing
a big game that was out there,

1043
01:10:19,301 --> 01:10:22,040
doesn't mean I wasn't
playing a big game.

1044
01:10:24,141 --> 01:10:26,360
I just wasn't stupid enough
to let everyone know

1045
01:10:26,461 --> 01:10:28,320
because I didn't wanna get voted out.

1046
01:10:30,221 --> 01:10:31,900
And that's why I'm sitting here.

1047
01:10:35,161 --> 01:10:36,800
Well said.

1048
01:10:39,441 --> 01:10:40,520
Mm.

1049
01:10:45,461 --> 01:10:48,400
Alright, guys, well, you
should have enough information

1050
01:10:48,541 --> 01:10:51,400
to decide who deserves the
title of Sole Survivor

1051
01:10:51,541 --> 01:10:53,080
and the half million that goes with it.

1052
01:10:55,701 --> 01:10:58,720
Remember, tonight, you
are voting for a winner.

1053
01:11:00,921 --> 01:11:03,760
For the last time, it is time to vote.

1054
01:11:31,769 --> 01:11:33,588
OK, guys,

1055
01:11:33,729 --> 01:11:35,508
you should have enough information now

1056
01:11:35,649 --> 01:11:38,068
to decide who deserves the
title of Sole Survivor

1057
01:11:38,209 --> 01:11:39,548
and the half million that goes with it.

1058
01:11:42,069 --> 01:11:44,908
Remember, tonight, you
are voting for a winner.

1059
01:11:47,169 --> 01:11:50,268
For the last time, it is time to vote.

1060
01:11:51,929 --> 01:11:53,308
Shaun, you're up.

1061
01:13:11,789 --> 01:13:12,868
Good.

1062
01:13:30,149 --> 01:13:32,068
I'll go count the votes.

1063
01:13:51,869 --> 01:13:55,228
Guys, it's been an incredible season,

1064
01:13:55,369 --> 01:13:58,988
the only thing left to
do, Pia and Baden...

1065
01:13:59,089 --> 01:14:00,428
..is to read the votes.

1066
01:14:02,489 --> 01:14:06,708
But, a moment like this should be
shared with people you love the most.

1067
01:14:06,809 --> 01:14:07,828
Oh!

1068
01:14:09,469 --> 01:14:10,908
Come on in, guys.

1069
01:14:13,949 --> 01:14:16,128
Oh, my God, it's Lily.

1070
01:14:18,569 --> 01:14:20,428
Hello!

1071
01:14:20,529 --> 01:14:28,529
Hello.

1072
01:14:41,029 --> 01:14:43,028
Say hi to my friends.

1073
01:14:43,129 --> 01:14:44,348
Hello.

1074
01:14:45,949 --> 01:14:47,488
Say hi, Jamesy.

1075
01:14:55,089 --> 01:14:57,388
I can't believe that I'm here.

1076
01:14:57,489 --> 01:14:59,268
Can't believe this is happening.

1077
01:15:02,329 --> 01:15:06,988
Karen, how proud are you
of Baden right now?

1078
01:15:07,129 --> 01:15:09,868
- Extremely proud.
- Oh, Mum.

1079
01:15:10,009 --> 01:15:12,148
Especially after what
I watched last night.

1080
01:15:12,249 --> 01:15:16,708
What does it mean to see him
standing here on Day 50?

1081
01:15:16,849 --> 01:15:19,188
He's a changed person.

1082
01:15:19,289 --> 01:15:22,868
More confident, talking a lot more.

1083
01:15:24,969 --> 01:15:27,228
Even full of a bit of sass, last night.

1084
01:15:27,369 --> 01:15:29,388
Yeah.

1085
01:15:29,529 --> 01:15:31,628
I'm lost for words at the
moment, though. Jeez.

1086
01:15:34,749 --> 01:15:36,308
So Luke,

1087
01:15:36,449 --> 01:15:39,488
you think Pia deserves
to take this one out?

1088
01:15:41,209 --> 01:15:42,428
She...

1089
01:15:42,569 --> 01:15:45,308
I don't know, it's in the
hands of the jury, I guess.

1090
01:15:45,449 --> 01:15:49,588
Certainly... I'm just amazed
by everything she's achieved.

1091
01:15:52,409 --> 01:15:55,208
I can't get any prouder
of her at this point.

1092
01:15:55,289 --> 01:15:56,848
This is, to me, an affirmation

1093
01:15:56,969 --> 01:15:59,868
of everything that I've always
thought she's capable of.

1094
01:16:11,789 --> 01:16:15,348
Alright, guys, remember,
these votes are for a win.

1095
01:16:18,369 --> 01:16:20,268
I'm gonna read the votes.

1096
01:16:30,469 --> 01:16:32,108
First vote...

1097
01:16:32,209 --> 01:16:33,308
..Pia.

1098
01:16:44,969 --> 01:16:47,228
Pia. That's two votes Pia.

1099
01:16:55,369 --> 01:16:57,508
Pia. That's three votes Pia.

1100
01:17:07,649 --> 01:17:10,228
Pia. That's four votes Pia.

1101
01:17:27,549 --> 01:17:30,708
Winner of Australian Survivor, Pia.

1102
01:17:34,889 --> 01:17:37,068
Oh, Pia!

1103
01:17:38,209 --> 01:17:41,748
Wow! Oh, my God, Pia.

1104
01:17:41,849 --> 01:17:43,588
That was amazing.

1105
01:17:47,669 --> 01:17:48,788
Oh, my God!

1106
01:17:51,169 --> 01:17:52,948
Thank you, guys!

1107
01:17:54,529 --> 01:17:57,148
I gave it my best shot.

1108
01:17:57,249 --> 01:17:59,308
The dream.

1109
01:17:59,409 --> 01:18:01,068
She deserves it.

1110
01:18:04,249 --> 01:18:06,868
Your mum is incredible. Yeah?

1111
01:18:06,969 --> 01:18:08,348
Pia?

1112
01:18:08,449 --> 01:18:10,428
Here's your cheque.

1113
01:18:10,569 --> 01:18:15,628
Congratulations, you are
Australia's Sole Survivor 2019.

1114
01:18:21,729 --> 01:18:23,388
Go, Pia.

1115
01:18:27,669 --> 01:18:30,988
I can't believe I won Survivor!

1116
01:18:35,829 --> 01:18:36,948
I'm overwhelmed.

1117
01:18:37,089 --> 01:18:41,548
I just paid off my mortgage in
seven traumatising weeks.

1118
01:18:41,689 --> 01:18:44,288
Your mummy did such a great job.

1119
01:18:44,369 --> 01:18:46,068
My kids love Survivor

1120
01:18:46,209 --> 01:18:48,548
so to have them there
to see their mum win,

1121
01:18:48,689 --> 01:18:51,388
I'm so grateful that they
could share it with me.

1122
01:18:51,529 --> 01:18:55,708
This was the most amazing
experience in my life.

1123
01:18:55,809 --> 01:18:58,428
This is my friend Dave. Say hi.

1124
01:18:58,529 --> 01:19:00,388
I'm bonded with those people for life

1125
01:19:00,529 --> 01:19:03,868
and I've come away from
this a better person.

1126
01:19:03,969 --> 01:19:07,108
High five. Yee, boy!

1127
01:19:07,249 --> 01:19:09,648
Playing Survivor was a lifelong dream.

1128
01:19:09,769 --> 01:19:13,008
I always said that I was gonna
be first person voted out

1129
01:19:13,129 --> 01:19:16,388
or I would win and I
actually won!

1130
01:19:23,649 --> 01:19:27,648
Well, we went looking for Alibrandi
but I think we found Scarface.

1131
01:19:30,289 --> 01:19:33,908
You, for me, are the winner
of Sole Survivor in 2019.

1132
01:19:34,009 --> 01:19:35,348
Congratulations on that pitch.

1133
01:19:35,489 --> 01:19:37,708
I thought it was brilliant
so you've got my vote.

1134
01:19:37,849 --> 01:19:40,648
Your pitch has definitely
won it for me tonight.

1135
01:19:40,769 --> 01:19:43,508
I think you played a
great understated game.

1136
01:19:47,649 --> 01:19:51,288
Pia, wow, you played a
magnificent social game.

1137
01:19:51,369 --> 01:19:53,428
You surprised me big-time tonight.

1138
01:19:53,569 --> 01:19:55,148
I think you played a very subtle game,

1139
01:19:55,249 --> 01:19:57,228
um, I don't think you're a goat.

1140
01:19:57,329 --> 01:19:59,028
Congratulations, Pia.

1141
01:19:59,169 --> 01:20:02,308
I hope you enjoy the
title of Sole Survivor

1142
01:20:02,409 --> 01:20:03,788
'cause you've earnt it.

1143
01:20:03,929 --> 01:20:06,908
I have loved, loved, loved
playing this game with you.

1144
01:20:07,049 --> 01:20:10,508
You deserve it, you're
an amazing player.

1145
01:20:10,649 --> 01:20:13,648
You owe me dinner and a
night out with my family.

1146
01:20:13,729 --> 01:20:15,268
Alright.

